  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05. All 13 items are closed and every patient who wrote got a reply.\n- pt-0026 Hayes: lisinopril 20 mg renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0001). Last valid potassium was 4.6 on a 4/14 BMP; the 10/5 potassium of 6.1 was hemolyzed. Repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0002). Her two messages were handled as one request.\n- pt-0027 Odum: lisinopril 10 mg renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0003). Last valid potassium was 4.5 on a 1/20 BMP; the outside 8/27 potassium of 5.9 was hemolyzed. Repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0005). Amlodipine 5 mg renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004).\n- pt-0028 Park: lisinopril 10 mg given as a 30-day supply with 0 refills (mr-t0006) and a BMP ordered (sr-t0007), because her last BMP was 10/2/2025, more than 12 months ago. Metformin NOT refilled: her most recent valid eGFR is 39 (corrected 7/20 result; first reported as 51). Urgent task to PCP (task-t0008, about mr-00287). The task text gives the result id as obs-00277 by mistake; the correct id is obs-02077, and this is noted on the closed inbox item.\n- pt-0029 Brooks: lisinopril NOT refilled. Her creatinine rose 37.8% within 4 weeks of the 9/21 dose increase, which the protocol treats like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. Urgent task to PCP due today (task-t0009, about mr-00291); she has been out of lisinopril since 10/20. Metformin 1000 mg given as a 30-day supply with 0 refills (mr-t0010) and an HbA1c ordered (sr-t0011). Her last HbA1c was collected 4/14, more than 6 months ago.\n- pt-0030 Price: lisinopril 20 mg renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0012). Potassium was 5.2 and creatinine rose 23.6% after the dose increase, under the 30% limit. Metformin 1000 mg renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0013), using an outside HbA1c from 8/19. His three messages were handled as one decision per drug.\n- pt-0031 Webb: lisinopril 10 mg given as a 30-day supply with 0 refills (mr-t0014) and a BMP ordered (sr-t0015), because his last BMP was 10/20/2025, more than 12 months ago. Metformin 500 mg renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0016); the 10/14 eGFR of 39 was entered in error, so 92 from 9/28 counts.\nNo existing orders were held or stopped, apart from the old orders replaced by the renewals.",
